    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I need to clarify the responsibilities for a contract we are reviewing. We're looking at a shipment of electronic components from South Korea to Germany under CIF Incoterms 2020. Can you explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF (Cost, Insurance, and Freight) Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for delivering the goods to the named point of destination, ensuring that the goods are properly packed and labeled, providing a commercial invoice that includes the full value of the goods, and arranging for the loading of the shipment onto the vessel or carrier. The seller must also obtain insurance coverage for the goods during transit, and bear the risk of loss or damage to the goods prior to the point of destination. However, the seller is not responsible for the costs of transportation, customs clearance, or the delivery of the goods to the seller-designated customs agent.",
      "source": "target",
